; CSV's transducer part: the document's JSON events from the csv grammar's
; rule passes, for a host that reads parser events (alchemy-cli's
; `translate` and `run --grammar csv`, aless's export). The walk of the
; grammar's value under its default options is an array of one object
; per record after the first, keyed by the first record's cells, the
; header, and every event here is the one that walk gives. The library's
; `transduce-records` makes them, which a host's routers may run
; natively; this part is its spec.
;
; The passes: `csv` opens and closes the document; `record` opens and
; closes each record (a blank line is none, with `record.empty` off); a
; cell's `val` closes with the cell's value, a quoted field's text, an
; unquoted field's text with the spaces it holds, or what the grammar
; resolved it to where its options type a cell. An empty cell is a pass
; whose alternate the grammar puts in the group `empty`: an `elem` that
; opens without pushing a `val`, before a separator, and an `elem` whose
; close gives its token back at the record's end; it holds the empty
; string (`field.empty`). `list`, `newline` and `text` pass by. A
; record's cells are keyed by the header's cells in order, a cell past
; the header's width by `field~` and its position (the grammar's
; `field.nonameprefix`), and a header cell a record lacks holds the
; empty string. A header name repeated is streamed twice, as the record
; spells it, where the walk keeps the last value: the tree contract a
; host puts after the part refuses it, and the host reads the document
; whole.
def csv-transduce [input]
  transduce-records
    record
      entry :document "csv"
      entry :record "record"
      entry :cell "val"
      entry :empty "empty"
      entry :header true
      entry :unnamed "field~"
    input
